35,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It seems we have a real issue with sustainability. I found that joint clinics can collapse if budget and rota responsibilities aren't clearly owned, and external data agreements are taking over a year to finalize.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My findings suggest that while some initiatives, like the call-back trial, showed genuine success in reducing readmissions for the elderly, the benefits vanished the moment the program ended. Consistency seems to be our greatest challenge.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The staffing situation is uneven. Ward nursing vacancies are rising, and agency costs are climbing, but the midwifery rota currently has unusual slack. Therapy staffing is also declining as physiotherapists leave for the city.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The budget is tighter than we think; the development allocation is down by a quarter, and we're now paying for floor fitting out of that same pot. We must be realistic about the scale of our ambitions.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I am worried that our lovely hospital is already quite breathless. The car park fills up so early, and our booking system doesn't even see the work that happens without a fixed appointment.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, if the budget is that tight, we really can't afford a project that collapses after a year. We need something with a very clear, single point of ownership to ensure it lasts.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, I agree. It would be a shame to see another promising result, like the reduction in elderly readmissions, simply drift away because we lacked a permanent structure to support it.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, given the budget cuts, we should avoid any program that requires hiring more ward nurses or physiotherapists. We simply don't have the staff to support it without relying on expensive agency cover.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, your point is noted, but we must also consider the revenue. I found that only on-site sessions draw regional fund tariffs. Any program operating off-site is essentially a donation of our dwindling resources.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, that is a very important point. If we must keep things on-site for the funds, we must be extra careful. Our parking and rooms are already so full; we wouldn't want to crowd out our patients.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, that is a very good point. If we are limited to on-site work due to funding, we must ensure the program doesn't rely on external partners who might not sign the necessary data agreements in time.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, if the physical space is so constrained, perhaps we should prioritize a program that optimizes existing patient flows rather than one that adds new, heavy traffic to our halls.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, I agree. We should also consider the current staffing distribution. Since the midwifery rota has slack, a program that utilizes that capacity would be more sustainable than one adding pressure to the wards.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, utilizing existing slack is a logical move. However, let's not forget that any ""optimization"" that requires new floor fitting will eat into our already reduced development budget. We need a lean, on-site solution.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, it is lovely that we have some breathing room in midwifery. If we can find a way to help our patients without making the hallways too crowded or the parking lot more frantic, that would be wonderful.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree with everyone. To summarize, we need a lean, on-site program with a single owner that avoids external data hurdles and utilizes existing staff slack rather than adding to the ward vacancies.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I concur. We must ensure that whatever we choose is not merely a temporary trial, but a permanent improvement that respects our current staffing and spatial limits.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. A program that aligns with our current staffing strengths and avoids increasing the agency bill is the only sustainable path forward.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"It seems we have reached a consensus on the constraints. We require a project that is fiscally lean, generates on-site revenue, and avoids the pitfalls of staffing shortages or spatial congestion. Let us see if any candidates actually meet these criteria.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with you all. Let us hope for a proposal that is gentle on our staff and our space, so that everyone can continue to receive the care they deserve in a peaceful way.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
