59,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Looking at the options, I am very concerned about A and C. They rely on off-site work and external providers, which means funding risks and those long data agreement delays I found.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Midori. Candidate A reminds me of the shared nursing round, where weather and access issues caused many missed visits. It seems too fragile to be a permanent success.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Candidate B is problematic because it requires physiotherapists, and my review showed a steady drain of those staff to the city. Candidate D, however, utilizes the slack in the midwifery rota.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Candidate A and C are non-starters; they operate off-site and thus generate no regional fund tariffs. Candidate B requires new floor fitting and staff we don't have. Candidate D is the only logical choice.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Shion. Candidate D is a lovely choice; it uses the midwifery slack Misaki mentioned and, as a scheduled service, it will be much easier for our booking system to manage.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I agree that D is the most logical. However, I am slightly worried about the ""jointly delivered"" aspect. We must ensure the budget and rota are clearly owned so it doesn't collapse like the joint clinic I read about.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, that is a valid concern. However, since both midwifery and pediatrics are internal departments, the ownership should be far easier to define than with the external partners we've struggled with in the past.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Midori, I agree. As long as we leverage the existing midwifery capacity, the pressure on the pediatric side should be manageable. It is far safer than risking more agency spend on the wards.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Midori, the internal nature of the partnership minimizes the risk. More importantly, D is on-site, meaning it actually earns back through tariffs, unlike the others. It is the only option that doesn't bleed money.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I am sure our wonderful staff in midwifery and pediatrics will work together beautifully. Since it is a scheduled service, we can manage the flow so our parking lot doesn't become too frantic for the other patients.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,"That is very reassuring, Shizue. If we can manage the flow and ensure the internal ownership is clear, Candidate D seems to be the most harmonious and sustainable choice for everyone.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. Candidate D avoids the fragility of off-site visits and the staffing gaps of the other options. It is a stable path that allows us to build something lasting without overextending our resources.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Candidate D is the only proposal that aligns with our current staffing reality. It utilizes available capacity rather than exacerbating the vacancies and agency costs that are currently straining our budget.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"The logic is undeniable. Candidate D is the only proposal that respects our reduced budget, generates necessary revenue, and utilizes existing staff slack. Any other choice would be a calculated failure.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with you all. Candidate D is a gentle way to grow, supporting new parents without overwhelming our dear staff or crowding our hallways. It feels like the most peaceful and practical path forward.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,I am happy we have found a solution that balances our needs. I vote for Candidate D.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I believe Candidate D is the most resilient and sustainable option. It avoids the pitfalls of our past trials and respects our current limits. I vote for Candidate D.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Misaki,,Candidate D is the only choice that respects our staffing constraints and avoids increasing our agency costs. I vote for Candidate D.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,Candidate D is the only option that is fiscally responsible and operationally viable. It is the only choice that doesn't ignore the reality of our budget. I vote for Candidate D.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,It has been such a pleasure talking with you all. I am very happy that we have found a way to help our new parents while keeping our hospital peaceful. I vote for Candidate D.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
